During the PoC phase, our primary focus was on proving the CI/CD-based onboarding flow using Apigee, which we executed well. However, in a few areas we could have explored alternative approaches alongside the core implementation:

* For API onboarding, we mainly followed the standard CI/CD pipeline approach, but we could have evaluated more autonomous or semi-automated options (e.g., agent-based workflows) to reduce manual intervention.
* We focused on validating the current architecture, but didn’t fully explore whether a more flexible or scalable pattern could better align with future product and design roadmap needs.
* There was limited exploration of emerging approaches (e.g., AI-driven or agentic solutions) which, while not fitting perfectly into our current structure, could offer efficiency gains worth assessing early.

My suggestion is not to deviate from the PoC goal, but to allocate some space during such phases to evaluate innovative or alternative patterns that could influence longer-term direction.

